// Package webtag/test/dbintegration is an isolated Go module that hosts
// the dbintegration test suite. It lives outside the main webtag module
// so testcontainers-go and its ~40 transitive Docker / logrus dependencies
// never enter the production dependency graph — `go build ./...` and the
// shipped binary stay lean.
//
// The module imports back into the main webtag tree via the `replace`
// directive below; this is the standard nested-module pattern Go has
// supported since 1.18. The `internal/` packages on the main module are
// still visible because Go's internal-import rule operates on the import
// path ("webtag/test/dbintegration" sits under "webtag/", so it counts
// as a descendant of "webtag/internal/..."'s parent).
//
// To run the suite:
//
//	go test -C test/dbintegration -tags=dbintegration -count=1 ./...
//
// or
//
//	cd test/dbintegration && go test -tags=dbintegration -count=1 ./...
//
// Docker is required (the suite boots a real Postgres container via
// testcontainers-go).
module webtag/test/dbintegration

go 1.26

toolchain go1.26.6

require (
	github.com/gin-gonic/gin v1.12.0
	github.com/google/uuid v1.6.0
	github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 v5.10.0
	github.com/pgvector/pgvector-go v0.4.1
	github.com/riverqueue/river v0.43.0
	github.com/riverqueue/river/riverdriver/riverpgxv5 v0.43.0
	github.com/testcontainers/testcontainers-go/modules/postgres v0.42.0
	webtag v0.0.0
)

